---
name: credential-vocabulary
backends: [int, js]
---

# Credential names a secret's SOURCE and never carries the secret.

`std/credential.ssc` is the outbound half of `std.auth`: it declares where a token comes from so an
emitter has nothing to bake into a generated binary or bundle.

The load-bearing case here is the third one. `credentialEnv("HOME")` is constructed while `HOME` is
set to a real value in every environment this runs in, and its `source` must still be the **name**
`HOME` — never the expansion. If anyone makes construction eager "for convenience", resolution moves
from the target back into the emitting process, which is precisely the defect this type exists to
prevent, and this line turns into a machine-dependent path.

[credentialEnv, credentialFile, credentialLiteral, credentialNone, credentialBasic, withScheme](std/credential.ssc)

```scalascript
def show(c: Credential): String = c.kind + "|" + c.source + "|" + c.scheme

println(show(credentialEnv("ROZUM_TOKEN")))
println(show(credentialBasic("ROZUM_TOKEN")))
println(show(credentialEnv("HOME")))
println(show(credentialNone))
println(show(credentialLiteral("s3cr3t")))
println(show(withScheme(credentialFile("/etc/tok"), "Token")))
```
